Problem Statement
Develop a Mini Task Management Web Application using Java and
Spring Boot with database connectivity and frontend integration.
1. Database Design
Design a Task table with the following fields:
•	id (Primary Key)
•	title (Not Null)
•	description
•	priority (LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH)
•	status (TODO / IN_PROGRESS / DONE)
•	dueDate (Not Null)
•	createdAt (Auto Generated)
•	deleteFlag (for soft delete)

2. Backend Development
Implement the following REST APIs:
•	POST /tasks – Create new task.
•	GET /tasks – Retrieve all tasks.
•	GET /tasks/{id} – Retrieve task by ID.
•	DELETE /tasks/{id} – Delete task by ID.
•	PUT /tasks/{id}/status – Update task status.
•	GET /tasks/filter?priority=HIGH – Filter by priority.
•	GET /tasks/overdue – Retrieve overdue tasks (dueDate < today and status not DONE).

*Return meaningful error responses, http status codes,
add validations and exception handling.
*You can create any other necessary APIs as per frontend requirements
3. Frontend Integration
•	Create a form to add/update a task, with proper validations.
•	Display all tasks in a tabular format with delete and edit buttons.
•	Add pagination for listing tasks,
•	Add filter by priority.
5. Additional Requirements
•	Implement deletion of tasks via property (hard delete/ soft delete).
•	Add search by title and sorting by due date for tasks.
•	Create custom exception classes and implement request/response object mapping.